{"title":"2026 Indonesia District MO Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The amount of integers between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/3/1437ad45f3a23e5d6ff330cdc6771b378d0ff047.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$456$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/1/e513adf78ee28ac3403e90a42259bc55f59e2d8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2026$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> inclusive that can be written as a number with increasing digits from left to right is...\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We want a number whose digits are ordered in increasing order from left to right. We can divide this into three cases:\n</p>\n<ul><li><b>Case 1: 3-digit number</b></li></ul>\n<p>Since if we have some numbers in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/b/8abf50741a85a94f00d6d0bbb994f25b7ad47415.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{0,1,2,3\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" />, that would mean one of them would have to be in the hundreds digit, which is clearly less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/3/1437ad45f3a23e5d6ff330cdc6771b378d0ff047.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$456$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />. So, we'll choose 3 digits from the set not containing those digits, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/2/a02f77dfa3ef4cd53b179bf88f41774727a8c796.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{4,5,6,7,8,9\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"115\" height=\"20\" />. This can be evaluated as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/5/e85e365adcc2ae808c009a84b5585b2ab96f4bc1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{6}{3}=\\frac{6!}{3!3!}=\\boxed{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"149\" height=\"55\" />\n</p>\n<ul><li><b>Case 2: 4-digit number starting with 1</b></li></ul>\n<p>Notice that we only have to choose a 3-digit increasing number that does not contain any number from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/3/b03b58393f926f96a7429fdd1a588f37b8304c14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{0,1\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" />. We now only have to choose 3 digits from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/f/23f8440824a9efceca3bac830578ab38c27957f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{2,3,4,5,6,7,8,9\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"146\" height=\"18\" />, which can be evaluted as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/4/9640e56e0fc7e7f4cd68f7a442ea74968dfefcb5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{8}{3}=\\frac{8!}{5!3!}=\\boxed{56}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"149\" height=\"55\" />\n</p>\n<ul><li><b>Case 3: 4-digit number starting with 2</b></li></ul>\n<p>The problem asks for numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/f/f5fecc49a623234fd3805853bb60e878c4669e1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\le 2026$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"57\" height=\"16\" />. But the lowest number with increasing digits starting with 2 is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/a/a6ad6045f59b66f5de989d5f8f2a297b381f2aac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2345$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />. Hence, there are no numbers that satisfy this case.\n</p><p>The total amount of numbers from the three cases is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/f/72f5868033152a6f7670f7309511f17e43106d73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20+56=\\boxed{76}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"114\" height=\"25\" />\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO\" title=\"2026 Indonesia District MO\">2026 Indonesia District MO </a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems\" title=\"2026 Indonesia District MO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 Indonesia District MO Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2026 Indonesia District MO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2026 Indonesia District MO Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2026 Indonesia District MO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2026 Indonesia District MO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2026 Indonesia District MO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\